Subject: [PATCH] Make Metal runtime waits bounded and fail closed

Use bounded host waits with sticky asynchronous errors across Metal event,
queue, dependency, and staging paths. Retain the explicit producer completion
barrier before device-to-host copies and wait for the copy to complete before
publishing host bytes. Keep queue status tied to tracked validation and host
completion, and bound literal pattern expansion before falling back to the
existing loop.
